# Git workflow for this repo

After finishing a coherent set of code changes in this project:

1. `git fetch` / `git pull --ff-only` on `main` (merge only if fast-forward is not possible and the user expects it).
2. Create a commit with a clear message (why over what).
3. `git push` to `origin/main` (or the active tracking branch).
4. Do not leave finished feature work uncommitted unless the user explicitly asks to wait.

Do not force-push to main. Do not skip hooks. Prefer the Python/WSL commit helper when PowerShell breaks heredocs.
